{"id":"05d80cd20b53d8a2","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-df-complete-metric.md","title":"Complete Metric Space","display":"df-complete-metric — Complete Metric Space","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-complete-metric","aliases":["58-df-complete-metric","Complete Metric Space"],"display":"df-complete-metric — Complete Metric Space","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-cauchy-sequence.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-complete-metric"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-complete-metric</span><span>Complete Metric Space</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-complete-metric — Complete Metric Space"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"69c159416e7381e2\" href=\"?note=69c159416e7381e2\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-cauchy-sequence.md\">../batch06/58-df-cauchy-sequence.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,d,s\\in V\">\\(X,d,s\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMetricCauchySequence}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMetricCauchySequence}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"69c159416e7381e2\" href=\"?note=69c159416e7381e2\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-cauchy-sequence.md\">../batch06/58-df-cauchy-sequence.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}complete\\text{-}metric}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\n\\forall s\\in X^\\omega\\;\n\\left(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMetricCauchySequence}_S(s,X,d)\n\\to\n\\exists x\\in X\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\n(N\\leq n\\to d(s(n),x)&lt;\\varepsilon)\n\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}complete\\text{-}metric}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CompleteMetric}_S(X,d)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\n\\forall s\\in X^\\omega\\;\n\\left(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMetricCauchySequence}_S(s,X,d)\n\\to\n\\exists x\\in X\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\n\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\n(N\\leq n\\to d(s(n),x)&lt;\\varepsilon)\n\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Convergence is stated with the same metric <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span>; the former unary convergence predicate lost this essential parameter.</li>\n<li>Banach and Hilbert completeness are specializations with additional linear structure.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Munkres, Topology</li>\n<li>Rudin, Principles of Mathematical Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2}